# Machine tooltips
becom.machine.pylon.type=Pylon
becom.machine.pylon.info=Carries a telephone line between Line Terminals. Works without power, even unloaded.
becom.machine.repeater.type=Pylon, Repeater
becom.machine.repeater.info=Regenerates the line signal, so line loss starts over. Takes power from a cable on any side.
becom.machine.router.type=Pylon, Router
becom.machine.router.info=Joins lines into a network, so any phone on it can dial any other. Takes power from a cable on any side.
becom.machine.pylon.span=Links to pylons up to %s times the shorter one's height away, %s links at most
becom.machine.pylon.wrench=Wrench a node, then another, to link them; again to unlink. Sneak to turn it.
becom.machine.pylon.controller=Top of the column
becom.machine.pylon.frames=Steel Frame Box, in a column below the head
becom.machine.power=Uses %s EU/t at %s while working
becom.machine.terminal.info=Where a telephone line starts or ends. Links to one Pylon Head and serves exactly one phone.
becom.machine.terminal.cable=Reaches its phone through up to %s blocks of Phone Cable
becom.machine.antenna.type=Antenna
becom.machine.antenna.info=Serves radios in range and repeats all 16 radio channels. Links to other antennas on its own, and carries calls between lines bridged onto them.
becom.machine.antenna.range=Reaches about %s blocks to Low on open ground (%s dB link budget). Height and hills matter.
becom.machine.antenna.bridge=Wrench it to a Pylon Head or Line Terminal within %s blocks to bridge that line, %s bridges at most
becom.machine.antenna.controller=Top of the mast
becom.machine.antenna.mast=%s, in a mast below the head
becom.machine.antenna.hatch=Any base casing
becom.machine.transceiver.info=A radio on a block. Hold push-to-talk within reach to transmit through it; its loudspeaker plays its channel.
becom.machine.transceiver.range=Reaches about %s blocks directly. Talk within %s blocks; the loudspeaker carries %s.
becom.machine.me_bridge.info=Joins its ME network to BeCom's, so ME Phones on it can call any phone. Takes ME cable on any side and one channel.
becom.machine.me_bridge.link=Wrench-link it to a BeCom node within %s blocks.
becom.machine.videophone.info=A video speakerphone for wired networks. Give it Phone Cable to a Line Terminal, like a Telephone.
becom.machine.videophone.room=Everyone within %s blocks is in its call, and its loudspeaker carries %s. It hangs up after %s s with nobody near.
becom.videophone.step_closer=Stand within %s blocks of the Videophone to use it: its calls are for the people around it.

